 -- The Krauken Project <dneumann@arpio.io>  Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:15:00 -0400

krauken (0.1.30) stable; urgency=medium

  * Added a derivative term to the beer-temp cascade -- genuinely PID now,
    not PI. Confirmed live (fermentation 3's Free Rise stage) that P+I
    alone leaves real ramp-tracking headroom unused once
    INTEGRAL_MAX_F_H saturates on a fast-moving ramp target (beer lagging
    3.5F behind, chamber pinned well short of the safety envelope). Two
    alternatives were tried first and rejected by direct simulation, not
    assumption: back-calculation anti-windup against the internal ceiling
    actually recovers SLOWER than the existing plain clamp; dropping that
    ceiling for textbook conditional-integration against the real
    actuator envelope is correct and safe but makes a realistic transient
    WORSE (more overshoot), since the real envelope is far wider than the
    disturbance-sized internal ceiling.
  * The derivative term reacts to beer's own closing rate relative to the
    TARGET's own observed rate of change (not raw d(beer)/dt, which would
    permanently brake throughout any real ramp) -- verified this leaves
    sustained-disturbance steady-state tracking essentially untouched
    (exotherm/Cold Crash: ~0F error, same as before) while cutting
    Free Rise-style ramp lag by roughly 25% and reducing a real startup
    transient's overshoot by roughly 44%, both confirmed by simulation
    against real recorded data before shipping.
  * Required two additional pieces, each verified necessary by direct
    testing against a real recorded sensor-settling artifact from this
    exact fermentation (a 5.75F swing in under 2 minutes): the raw
    closing-rate signal is clamped to a physically-plausible maximum
    before it's ever filtered (no real beer thermal mass could produce
    what that artifact implied), and the low-pass filter itself uses a
    multi-hour time constant, not the minutes typical PID tutorials use --
    both were independently confirmed necessary; neither alone was
    sufficient to keep the artifact from slamming the commanded chamber
    target toward the safety envelope.
  * New constants: BEER_KD_F_PER_F_PER_H, CLOSING_RATE_FILTER_TAU_H,
    MAX_PLAUSIBLE_BEER_RATE_F_PER_H (contracts/control_constants.py).

