krauken (0.1.17) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the BrewPi setup wizard's probe-identification screen (deviceProbeId)
    flashed a false "No {chamber|beer} probe detected" on every job-to-job
    transition -- a freshly-started identify_onewire_probes job legitimately
    reports state:"running", result:null for one or two polls (real serial
    I/O latency, not a bug) before its first real reading lands, and the
    render logic treated that null result as "zero probes found." Reproduced
    live this session on entering the stage and again right after confirming
    the chamber probe.
  * Fix: the beer/chamber probe screen's Continue button waited out the
    backend's fast-path settle loop (up to ~2s) after a reading had already
    come back valid, purely because that loop only existed to eventually
    flip the job to "completed" -- unrelated to whether the frontend already
    knew enough to continue.
  * Fix: the hardware setup wizard's dialog visibly resized on every stage
    transition (including automatic ones) because its container only had a
    max-height, so it shrink-wrapped to each stage's actual content. Given a
    fixed width/height instead, with the content area taking the remaining
    space and scrolling internally for any stage tall enough to exceed it.
  * Redesigned deviceProbeId as a list of selectable probe cards instead of
    separate zero/one/many-candidate branches: chamber phase requires an
    explicit candidate (no probe found means Retry/Cancel, never a bare
    Continue -- BrewPi cannot function without a chamber probe); a lone
    candidate is auto-selected immediately (nothing to compare against);
    multiple candidates auto-select on a real 3F warm-up but can also just
    be tapped directly; beer phase adds an explicit "No beer probe" card
    among the real candidates rather than a separate skip link, and its own
    lone candidate is never auto-selected by presence alone (only by
    actually warming it or tapping it), since a beer probe is optional and
    genuinely may not exist. Removed the now-unreachable deviceNoProbe stage
    that this replaces.
  * Moved all probe warm-detection out of the backend and into the wizard:
    identify_onewire_probes (device_config.py) no longer computes a delta or
    an identified_address at all -- it only surfaces baseline_f/current_f/
    readable on a fixed poll interval, and HardwareWizard.tsx does its own
    delta-vs-threshold check against those same fields. This also lets a
    single beer-phase candidate auto-select by warming, which the backend's
    old single-candidate fast path never compared a delta for at all. Since
    the job no longer self-terminates on a match, the wizard now explicitly
    cancels it before advancing past this screen instead of relying on it
    having already completed.
  * Wizard copy pass across the BrewPi device-configuration flow: replaced
    low-level "pin N" language with "outlet controller N+/-" (polarity
    folded into the label, never shown without those words) throughout the
    relay-identification sweep and the final summary; reworded the intro,
    heat-sweep interstitial, no-cooling, and finalize screens toward plain,
    outlet/probe-centric language instead of internal implementation detail.

 -- The Krauken Project <dneumann@arpio.io>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:57:07 -0400

krauken (0.1.16) stable; urgency=high

  * Fix (safety): finalize_device_config could leave the heater genuinely
    on after completing successfully. Confirmed live on the real rig via
    strace: the correct off-polarity heat install was sent and echoed
    back correctly by the firmware, but the immediately-following `R`
    reset landed only ~0.3s later (the standard per-install settle) --
    not reliably enough margin before a hard reset specifically, which
    (unlike a normal follow-up command) doesn't wait for an in-flight
    EEPROM write to actually commit. Real, direct evidence: two separate
    devices in the same finalize batch (a probe's OneWire address, and
    the heat relay's invert) both came back different from what was just
    written and correctly echoed, immediately after the reset. New
    FINALIZE_VERIFY_RETRIES: before ever sending R, finalize now reads
    back and verifies every pushed device actually matches what was
    intended, retrying a few times first -- both closing the race (a
    real round trip is genuine settle time) and catching a miss instead
    of trusting it blindly. Best-effort past the retry budget (logged,
    not fatal) -- the reset always still happens either way.
  * Fix: _slot_for() (used by finalize_device_config to decide whether to
    reuse an existing slot or pick a fresh one) matched entries in the
    AVAILABLE list by address, not just genuinely installed ones --
    every available entry always reports slot -1 (list_all_devices() is
    installed+available combined), so a probe being installed for the
    first time (the ordinary case) got sent to the Arduino as "i":-1.
    Confirmed live: DeviceManager.cpp silently rejects that (no response
    at all), so the beer probe never actually got installed. Only a
    genuinely installed device's slot is ever reused now.

